list.item:
Foods containing a large amount of protein as  compared with the fuel value.

Fish;

veal;

lean beef, such as shank, shoulder, canned corned, round, neck, and chuck;

skim milk.

Foods containing a medium amount of protein.

Fowl;

eggs;

mutton leg and shoulder;

beef, fatter cuts, such as rib, loin, rump, flank, and brisket;

whole milk;

beans and peas;

mutton chuck and loin;

cheese;

lean pork;

oatmeal and other breakfast foods;

flour;

bread, etc.

Foods containing little or no protein.

Vegetables and fruit;

fat pork;

rice;

tapioca;

starch;

butter and other fats and oils;

sugar, syrups.
